// SWARM RABBIT HOLE — Wave 8 (Impl-L): GC scoping — the E-GC-IN-LANE
// fail case, lane→GC direction (the inverse confusion). D0 gap #6 /
// W2A §1.4: a lane-backed binding's bytes die at the lane rewind — the
// lane is reset without consulting anything else — while the GC-managed
// holder (sn_obj_new → gc_track) persists. A lane reference stored into
// the surviving GC object dangles the moment the lane rewinds: same
// category-confusion hazard, opposite direction.
//
// 'lane_cell' is lane-backed (explicit `lane_alloc`, lane_of); 'h' is
// GC-managed (the `new` constructor path). Storing a ref to 'lane_cell'
// into 'h's field must fire E-GC-IN-LANE at the T-STORE site (dst root
// 'h'). The store is also a stack escape (the existing dangling-stack
// rule fires alongside) — both diagnostics are honest: the store is
// BOTH a scope escape AND a collector-category confusion.
//
// Compile-FAIL golden case (tests/golden.rs): [E-GC-IN-LANE].

blueprint Holder {
    ptr cell
}

fn main() {
    ptr lane_cell = lane_alloc(2, 64)
    new Holder h()
    h.cell = address(lane_cell)
}
